  "identity": {
    "playing_style": "Emery's Villa defend in a compact 4-4-2 mid-block out of a 4-2-3-1, build patiently through short passes to lure the opposition press and then break lines vertically, and attack narrow with full-backs providing overlapping width. A double pivot (Kamara with Onana or, from 2026/27, Joao Gomes/Goretzka) screens the back four. After the 2026 sale of ball-carrier Morgan Rogers the club has explicitly bought Johan Manzambi as the carrier and Garnacho/Mbaye for pace and dribbling.",
    "principles": [
      "coach-led, meticulous game-plan football under long-serving Emery",
      "profit-from-sales model imposed by UEFA squad-cost-ratio settlement",
      "buy high-ceiling U23 profiles with resale value (Manzambi 20, Mbaye 18, Suzuki 24, Ruggeri 24) balanced by experienced free/loan signings (Goretzka, Wan-Bissaka)",
      "academy players monetised (most made available for sale in summer 2026)"
    ],
    "club_character": "Historic founder member of the Football League, single-club city rivalry with Birmingham City, large traditional working-class fanbase at Villa Park (stand redevelopment ongoing). Expectations now high after 2026 Europa League win (first trophy in 30 years) and back-to-back top-4 finishes; heavy press scrutiny in Sept 2026 over the sale of Rogers, Konsa, Watkins and Tielemans.",
    "ownership": "Private: V Sports (Nassef Sawiris and Wes Edens ~34.4% each, US investment firm Atairos ~32% minority stake). Chairman Nassef Sawiris.",
    "political_and_social_context": "Publicly documented: the club operates under a UEFA financial settlement (total exposure EUR 48.5m: EUR 18.5m unconditional, EUR 30m conditional on squad-cost-ratio improvement) for breaching UEFA financial rules; UEFA rejected GBP 114m of intra-group asset sales (women's team, training-ground 'Warehouse') that the Premier League accepted for PSR. In July 2026 the club made almost all academy players available for sale to comply with spending rules. Summer 2026 saw a club-record GBP 120m sale of Morgan Rogers and gross sales of roughly GBP 300m+.",
    "languages": [
      "en",
      "es",
      "fr",
      "pt"
    ],
    "wage_structure": "hierarchical - top band around GBP 8m/yr gross (Kamara, Martinez; Tielemans before sale); total 2026/27 wage bill approx GBP 118.5m, 7th in the Premier League (Capology estimate)",
    "transfer_policy": "Forced net-seller in 2026 (net profit >GBP 100m); sells peak-value stars, reinvests in U25 resale-value profiles plus free/loan veterans; Emery has strong influence on targets",
    "injury_management_reputation": "Publicly discussed workload: Amadou Onana ruptured an ACL at the 2026 World Cup (out to ~April 2027) and Manzambi arrived with a World Cup knee injury; Emery's staff have been praised for rotation across a 60+ game season but no systematic criticism of the medical department was found."
  },
